//** 
How it works, step by step:

Playwright starts a test.
The test uses a locator from the locator map.
If the locator works, the test continues normally.
If the locator breaks, the AI healing layer reads the current open page through Playwright.
It checks the live DOM, page text, page title, and page scope.
It tries to repair the locator.
If healing succeeds, it saves the fixed selector into the override cache so next runs use the better locator.
If you enable the MCP backup, the test can also ask the MCP server for help when local healing does not solve it.


So the logic is:

normal run = use the locator map
broken locator = try AI healing from the live page
if enabled = use MCP server as backup
saved fix = written to locator-overrides.json
**/